Z||000019||mrfixit58||09-29-2001||09:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>it's never been tested - it is a 3.4 Twin Dual Cam throttle body matted up to a stock intake. It is intended to be used for a 3.4 push-rod engine, but no one has ever stepped up to the plate<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You mean there's no one near Marina Del Rey, CA, with a 3.4 is will to test that thing? If you find a volunteer, how will you test it? On a dyno... before and after kinda thing? You'll pay for everything? Maybe even offer a discount on one if they like the results -- you know, for there trouble?<P>Come on... isn't some one in that area who can help? I would like to see the results on paper.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
