Z||000048||chester||10-04-2001||02:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>where in the hell did I say that the intake costs $400, but we sure as hell aren't going to give it up for free, fuel management and ALL ,( All), did I say all, hardware and equipment are included.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dude,<P>I CALLED you about it when I saw the post on YOUR website.  WITHOUT the fuel mangement SOMEONE at your establishment (Eric maybe) told me $400. Hence, you never heard back from me.  <P>Rob D.<P>||||reg||13
Z||000049||Formula88||10-04-2001||02:43 PM||||Even so, since it's a prototype part, charging anything for it is ridiculous.  You want to test it?  Ask for volunteers.  They supply the vehicle, you supply the manpower and expertise.  When you've proven the system works, then put a price tag on it.  <P>Asking someone to buy a part that you have no idea if it'll work or not seems silly.  You shouldn't give it away, but you shouldn't expect people to line up to buy something that has no guarantee of working.  If you decide it works great and intend to produce them, you might offer the prototype or an early production unit to the person who let you use their car as a mule for a discount.<P>Besides, don't you guys have one of your own cars to test it on?  How do you test your other equipment?  Someone's gotta try it first, right?  If I were in the area, I'd allow you to test it on my car.  I'm not saying I'd buy it.  You could have it back when the testing was done, but I'd donate the use of my vehicle.  If it was really great, I'd probably buy it.||||reg||6
Z||000050||West Coast Fiero||10-04-2001||06:55 PM||||we have so many other projects going on right now such as a northstar conversion, turbo 3800, and manufacturing all of our products - testing an add on to a 3.4 let alone a 2.8 is not exactly at the top of the list. The thing is that this throttle body that is fabricated on to the 2.8 intake plenum is from a 3.4 Twin Dual Cam, you cannot buy the throttle body alone as it is cast into the intake of the TDC. As you can see this was NOT a cheap item to make - so it up for grabs to the first person that steps up to the plate<P><P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
