Z||000054||chester||10-05-2001||06:53 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B> <BR>with a 3.4 Twin Dual Cam throttle body with 3" intake welded and machine to fit on a 2.8?<P>I believe you are missing the point, and I get irratated when I have to repeat myself, esspecially when everything I have said is IN PRINT above<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dude,<P>First off your irritation stems from the illusion that someone would be willing to shell out hundreds of dollars for an untested prototype intake. IMO that is a ass backwards way of doing R&D.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> If you don't have the time to test the product, don't expect top dollar for it.  I'd suggest that either you lower the price or just simply get over it.  Second is if you decided to jump in on the ass end of a conversation make sure that you got your sh*t straight.  No I did not say I can get an upper plenum with your mod for $40.  I said that you can get a upper plenum that is stock (non engraved) for $40.  You guys just don't know when to give up. <P>Rob D.<P>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 10-05-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||1
